PRE-REGISTRATION -- the REWRITE arm: is description fidelity CAUSAL?     2026-09-12
Written at 11:57, BEFORE any rewrite is generated or scored. Pod is held by the
TOPK eval and the 03-lru determinism arms until ~14:40; this runs after.

WHAT IS ESTABLISHED (ADR-0158, merged 7ed0b90)
  Description fidelity -- per-skill token coverage of a skill's queries by its
  name+description -- predicts full-catalogue selection accuracy on two
  independent catalogues (rho +0.637 / +0.534; tertile spreads 50 / 34.6).
  Size, length and family size are falsified. NO causal claim was made: low
  coverage may CAUSE misses, or may merely MARK intrinsically ambiguous skills.
  Only an intervention separates those. This is that intervention.

THE TAUTOLOGY TRAP, and the holdout that avoids it
  Queries are paragraphs 2-4 of each skill's body (queries_for: paras[1:4] of
  the >200-char paragraphs). A rewriter shown the whole body would raise
  coverage of exactly those paragraphs BY CONSTRUCTION, and a lift would prove
  only that descriptions can be made to echo their queries.
  HOLDOUT: the rewriter sees the skill NAME, the ORIGINAL description, and the
  body with the three query-source paragraphs REMOVED. It never sees a query.
  Any coverage gain then comes from describing the skill better, not from
  copying the test. Skills with fewer than 2 long paragraphs left after the
  holdout are EXCLUDED and counted, not silently kept.

DESIGN
  Population: ayoai-mind, 140 skills, 420 queries -- the same set as every arm
  in this arc. Target: the LOWEST-coverage tertile (46 skills) by the measure in
  description_fidelity.py. Rewriter: zds-qwen3.6-35b at temperature 0 (the same
  model, so a Mind could run this autonomously; deterministic per ADR-0157), one
  call per skill, instructed to write a 1-3 sentence description of what the
  skill does and when to use it, from the holdout body.
  Arms, each the FULL 145-skill catalogue rendered identically:
    ORIG     original descriptions                      (control; must reproduce)
    REWRITE  the 46 target descriptions replaced; the other 94 untouched
  Both arms score ALL 420 queries: rewriting 46 descriptions changes the
  confusability of the other 94 too, and a rewrite that helps its targets by
  hurting the rest is a net loss that a targets-only score would hide.

PREDICTIONS, fixed before any rewrite exists
  W0 ORIG reproduces: FULL within 3 points of 60.2% (three prior runs: 60.2,
     60.2, 60.2). VOID below 45%.
  W1 (mechanism check, no model scoring needed) the rewritten descriptions have
     HIGHER coverage than the originals on at least 35 of the 46 targets. If the
     rewriter did not raise coverage, the arm is not a fidelity test at all.
  W2 (THE TEST) target-skill accuracy rises under REWRITE: paired bootstrap over
     the 46 target skills, two-sided 95% CI on (REWRITE - ORIG); point estimate
     >= +10 points, CI excludes zero. The targets sit at 35.5%; +10 is set well
     inside the predicted direction, not at it (guard-5645).
  W3 (non-inferiority of the untouched 94) their accuracy under REWRITE is not
     more than 5 points below ORIG -- the same margin as the retracted
     shortening run, in the same direction.
  W4 (direction only) the model picks a rewritten TARGET skill for a query
     belonging to an UNTOUCHED skill more often under REWRITE than ORIG --
     rewritten descriptions become more attractive decoys. Predicted, so it is
     not read as a surprise; W3 is what bounds it.

DECISION RULES
  W0 fails -> arm drifted; no verdict.
  W1 fails -> the rewriter did not change what it was meant to; NO verdict on
     causality, and do not rescue it by letting the rewriter see more body.
  W1 AND W2 AND W3 hold -> FIDELITY IS CAUSAL. The rewrite is a product action:
     file a goal to apply the same rewrite procedure to the real catalogue,
     fleet-wide, with the coach replication as the second check.
  W1 holds, W2 fails -> coverage rose and accuracy did not: fidelity is a
     MARKER of intrinsic ambiguity, not a cause. Retire the rewrite lever and
     say so in ADR-0158's addendum; the correlation stands, the remedy does not.
  W2 holds, W3 fails -> the lift is paid for by the untouched skills; report
     the net over all 140 and do not ship a rewrite that moves errors around.

WHAT THIS CANNOT DO
  One catalogue, one rewriter, one model. A causal result here licenses the
  coach replication as the next step, not a fleet rollout on its own.

=== 14:43 SCORE PHASE KILLED BY HAND -- the target set is contaminated by an instrument defect
W1 failed (coverage rose on 17/45, floor 35). Then: 11 of the 45 targets -- the entire lowest-coverage tertile's
bottom -- have orig == ">-". choosability_eval.py reads the description with ^description:\s*(.+)$, so a YAML
folded/literal block scalar ("description: >-" + indented lines) is read as the two-character indicator. Those 11
skills had coverage ~0 by artifact, sat in the catalogue the MODEL saw as ">-", scored FULL 0.364 vs 0.623 for the
other 129 and 0.091 in every TOPK arm (BM25 cannot retrieve a name-only entry). The score phase would have compared
rewritten real descriptions against ">-" for those 11 and manufactured a gain. Killed at 14:43:13; no W0-W4
verdicts from this pass are valid. Repair: parser fix + loader guard, then the fidelity and shortlisting numbers are
recomputed / re-measured under their own pre-registrations before any rewrite arm is re-attempted.

